# Given a global set before parallel_map,
# When built natively and the workers read it,
# Then they see it, as interpreted (where a global is one process-wide
# table). Each worker was handed an empty __globals instead, so it read
# false (raytrace ch37: fa_run never saw "fa_scratch", fell back to the
# main thread's vec handles, and rendered from or crashed on them).
include "../../lib/block_model_compat.patlang"
make a function called work takes item returns r
  return item + get_global("base")
end
set_global("base", 100)
print(parallel_map([1, 2, 3], "work"))
